# Routing

App Router. Server Components by default.

## Special files

- `page.tsx` — default export, async when fetching data in RSC
- `layout.tsx` — shared shell, receives `children`, persists across navigations
- `loading.tsx` — Suspense fallback, skeleton matching page shape
- `error.tsx` — error boundary, `'use client'`, receives `error` + `reset`
- `not-found.tsx` — 404 UI, triggered by `notFound()`
- `global-error.tsx` — root error boundary, `'use client'`
- `route.ts` — Route Handlers only for webhooks or OAuth callbacks, never UI data

## Route groups

- `(admin)`, `(auth)`, `(landing)`, `(protected)`, `(public)` — layout separation, no URL impact
- `[...not-found]` catch-all for 404 fallback

## Dynamic segments

- `[slug]/page.tsx` — access via `params` prop
- async params (Next 15+): `const { slug } = await params`
- `searchParams` also async: `const sp = await searchParams`

## Metadata

- static: `export const metadata: Metadata = { title, description }`
- dynamic: `generateMetadata({ params })` — param-based titles
- set at the deepest segment owning the title

## Runtime data in layouts

`cookies()`, `headers()`, `getSession()` block streaming. Extract to async child wrapped in `<Suspense>` — never in the layout body.

## Auth redirects

Route guards live in `src/proxy.ts`. Never perform auth logic in pages/layouts — call `requireAuth()` / `requireEmailVerification()` from `@/lib/auth/session` when the RSC needs the user.

## Rules

- page fetches data, passes to feature components as props — never fetch inside domain components
- never `'use client'` on `page.tsx` or `layout.tsx`
- co-locate `loading.tsx` next to the page that owns the slow fetch
